    57	 * **The claim is held open rather than answered empty.** Dispatch is pull,
    58	 * and the promise a developer actually feels is "a queued simulation is
    59	 * claimed within about a second". So an empty queue holds the request and
    60	 * re-asks every second until work arrives or the hold runs out — the long
    61	 * poll every pull-dispatch product ships. The client says how long it is
    62	 * willing to hang (`wait_seconds`), the server holds at most `min` of that
    63	 * and its own cap, and a client that said nothing gets a middling default —
    64	 * so a short-waiting client can never see its own request time out. A
    65	 * notification may one day replace the re-ask behind this same route;
